.\" Manual page for the Mitsuzo command-line client.
.TH MITSUZO 1 "2026-10-02" "mitsuzo 0.12.10" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mitsuzo \- client for the Mitsuzo encrypted paste service
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mitsuzo
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
\fICOMMAND\fR
[\fIARGS\fR]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mitsuzo
is the command-line client for Mitsuzo, a self-hostable service for sending
secrets and short-lived files. Encryption and decryption happen on the local
machine; only ciphertext and the metadata needed to deliver it are sent to the
server.
.PP
Running
.B mitsuzo
without a command prints usage. Pass
.B \-\-help
to any command for its options.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-b ", " \-\-base\-url " " \fIURL\fR
Base URL of the Mitsuzo server. Overrides the
.B base_url
value from the configuration file. Defaults to
.BR http://localhost:3030 .
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print version information.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS create
.B mitsuzo create
[\fB\-f\fR \fIFILE\fR] [\fB\-c\fR \fIN\fR] [\fB\-t\fR \fISECONDS\fR]
[\fB\-b\fR] [\fB\-T\fR \fIKID\fR]
.PP
Encrypt and upload a new paste and print its share identifier and link. The
secret is read from standard input unless
.B \-\-file
is given.
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-file " " \fIFILE\fR
Read the secret from
.I FILE
instead of standard input.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-try\-count " " \fIN\fR
Maximum number of read attempts. Default:
.BR 5 .
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-ttl " " \fISECONDS\fR
Time to live in seconds. Default:
.BR 43200
(12 hours).
.TP
.BR \-b ", " \-\-burn\-after\-read
Burn the paste after the first successful read.
.TP
.BR \-T ", " \-\-to " " \fIKID\fR
Encrypt for an existing account key identifier (a
.B 0x
prefix or a full hash) instead of a password. Only the matching account can
decrypt the paste.
.SS get
.B mitsuzo get
[\fB\-o\fR \fIFILE\fR]
\fIID\fR
.PP
Download and decrypt the paste identified by
.IR ID .
The decrypted content is written to standard output unless
.B \-\-output
is given.
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output " " \fIFILE\fR
Write the decrypted content to
.I FILE
.
.SS passwd
.B mitsuzo passwd
\fIID\fR
.PP
Change the password that protects the paste identified by
.IR ID .
The current and new passwords are read interactively.
.SS account
.B mitsuzo account
\fIACTION\fR
.PP
Manage the optional zero-knowledge account used for recipient-mode
encryption.
.SS "account register"
.B mitsuzo account register
\fB\-n\fR \fINAME\fR
.PP
Generate a new account, show a 24-word seed phrase once for backup, store the
locked key in
.IR ~/.config/mitsuzo/account.enc ,
and register the public key with the server.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-name " " \fINAME\fR
Account display name.
.SS "account login"
.B mitsuzo account login
.PP
Unlock the local account and print its profile.
.SS "account import"
.B mitsuzo account import
\fB\-n\fR \fINAME\fR
[\fIPHRASE\fR]
.PP
Recover a local account from an existing seed phrase. If
.I PHRASE
is omitted, it is read interactively from standard input.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-name " " \fINAME\fR
Account display name.
.SH CONFIGURATION
The server URL may be stored in a YAML configuration file:
.PP
.nf
.RS
base_url: https://mitsuzo.example.com
.RE
.fi
.PP
The following files are read in order until one is found:
.IP "1." 4
\fI$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/mitsuzo/config.yml\fR
.IP "2." 4
\fI~/.config/mitsuzo/config.yml\fR
.IP "3." 4
\fI/etc/mitsuzo/config.yml\fR
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/mitsuzo/config.yml
User configuration.
.TP
.I ~/.config/mitsuzo/account.enc
Locally stored, locked account key.
.TP
.I /etc/mitsuzo/config.yml
System-wide configuration.
.SH EXAMPLES
Encrypt a string from standard input:
.PP
.nf
.RS
echo "secret message" | mitsuzo create
.RE
.fi
.PP
Upload a file with a one-hour lifetime:
.PP
.nf
.RS
mitsuzo create \-\-file document.pdf \-\-ttl 3600
.RE
.fi
.PP
Retrieve a paste and save it to a file:
.PP
.nf
.RS
mitsuzo get 123456 \-\-output decrypted.pdf
.RE
.fi
.PP
Create an account, then encrypt a paste for it:
.PP
.nf
.RS
mitsuzo account register \-\-name alice
mitsuzo create \-\-to 0xabc123
.RE
.fi
